Patterns: SDD

Purpose:
  Define architecture patterns available for selection. AI MUST select
  a pattern based on project requirements, constraints, and trade-offs.

Patterns:

  Monolith:
    name: Monolith
    description: Single deployable application
    complexity: Low
    scale_fit: L0-L1
    pros:
      - simple deployment
      - easy development
    cons:
      - scaling limitations
      - team coordination challenges
    when_to_use:
      - small team, low traffic, simple domain, prototype/MVP
    when_to_avoid:
      - high traffic, multiple teams, complex domain

  ModularMonolith:
    name: Modular Monolith
    description: Single deployable with internal module boundaries
    complexity: Medium
    scale_fit: L1-L3
    pros:
      - simple deployment
      - clear module boundaries
      - can extract modules later
    cons:
      - scaling limited to whole app
    when_to_use:
      - medium team, medium traffic, clear domain boundaries
    when_to_avoid:
      - very high traffic, independent scaling needs

  Microservices:
    name: Microservices
    description: Multiple independently deployable services
    complexity: High
    scale_fit: L3-L5
    pros:
      - independent scaling
      - independent deployment
    cons:
      - operational complexity
      - network latency
    when_to_use:
      - large team, high traffic, clear domain boundaries
    when_to_avoid:
      - small team, low traffic, insufficient DevOps maturity

  EventDriven:
    name: Event-Driven Architecture
    description: Components communicate via events
    complexity: Medium-High
    scale_fit: L2-L5
    pros:
      - loose coupling
      - scalability
      - async processing
    cons:
      - eventual consistency
      - debugging complexity
    when_to_use:
      - async workflows, event sourcing, multiple consumers
    when_to_avoid:
      - simple CRUD, strong consistency required

  Serverless:
    name: Serverless
    description: Function-as-a-Service, no server management
    complexity: Medium
    scale_fit: L1-L4
    pros:
      - automatic scaling
      - pay-per-use
    cons:
      - cold starts
      - vendor lock-in
    when_to_use:
      - variable traffic, event-driven workloads, rapid prototyping
    when_to_avoid:
      - consistent high traffic, long-running processes

Note:
  CQRS, Event Sourcing, Hexagonal, Clean Architecture, and Layered
  are design patterns applied within modules, not system architecture
  patterns. Use them at module level, not as top-level architecture.

Selection:
  AI MUST select architecture pattern based on:
    ProjectScale (L0-L5), Team size, Domain complexity,
    Traffic patterns, Scaling requirements, Budget

  OverengineeringGate:
    AI MUST flag OVERENGINEERING when:
      pattern complexity > project scale justifies
      team size < pattern requires
      traffic < pattern requires

  UnderengineeringGate:
    AI MUST flag UNDERENGINEERING when:
      availability requirements > pattern provides
      security requirements > pattern provides
      traffic > pattern can handle

Navigation:
  Levels: @levels.sdd
  Principles: @principles.sdd

State: +
